/-!
# The faithful temporary core transvection argument

The conditional source interface proves the Frattini step for ⟨τ,Q⟩, commuting
residual and core action images, faithful common-center transvections on the
first marked fixed space, and fixed-codimension doubling for every subgroup
of the core action image. The adapter supplies both displayed offender rank
inequalities with B = A ∩ Q. The original lineV and original lineQ are retained;
the temporary two-core is recovered from the original local inputs.

`TemporaryData` and `FixedGeometry` expose the precise original local facts
and marked geometry that the replacement assembly must supply.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, proof of 15.3.67, printed pp.1153–1154,
combined manuscript (1 March 2004), PDF pp.1170–1171.
-/
